%description:

Tcp.icmpSequenceCheck:on -- an ICMP error with a stale sequence number is ignored: the SYN goes again.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: an ICMP error whose quoted TCP segment has a sequence number outside
SND.UNA to SND.MAX is ignored as stale or forged ...; false: each ICMP error of the connection
counts, as RFC 9293 section 3.9.2.2 says".

The classes: off (false, the default) and on (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::isIcmpErrorInWindow() ignores an ICMP error whose quoted segment has a sequence
number outside SND.UNA to SND.MAX, with true. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, behind a router, with softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup (precondition: an ICMP
error that counts then aborts the setup). The tap sets the TTL of the first SYN of host1 to 1
and its sequence number 100 higher, so the Time Exceeded of the router quotes a sequence number
outside SND.UNA to SND.MAX. Observation: level 1, host1 sends the SYN again after the timer of the SYN.

%# parameter: Tcp.icmpSequenceCheck
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.icmpSequenceCheck
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpIcmpSequenceCheckOn")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").nth(1)
                     .set("ipv4.timeToLive", "1").set("tcp.sequenceNo", "tcp.sequenceNo + 100")
                     .describe("the first SYN of host1: a TTL of 1 and a sequence number 100 higher"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the second SYN of host1, after the timer of the SYN")
             .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpIcmpSequenceCheckOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.icmpSequenceCheck = true    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.host1.tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup = true
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpIcmpSequenceCheckOn: PASS
